// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// REVIEW STATUS: UNVERIFIED. NOT LEGALLY CERTIFIED. NOT FOR PRODUCTION USE.
//
// Every declaration in this directory carries `review_status unverified`. The
// publication gate (`setuctl publish --production`) refuses to publish a
// ruleset containing unverified content, so this cannot reach an applicant by
// accident. It exists to exercise the engine end to end and to give the
// regulatory content team a worked, well-structured starting point.
//
// Before any of this becomes law-in-software, each rule must go through the
// four-eyes workflow of spec 5.5.5: author, legal reviewer, department
// sign-off. The thresholds and citations below were written from public
// sources by an engineer, not a lawyer, and several are known to be
// simplifications — they are flagged individually with a REVIEW note.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

